WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.840
I'm surprised.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.820
I guess you really can't judge a book by its cover.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.100
You're so hard.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.450
You're the one making me do this.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.120
Don't you want to?

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.200
I mean, I'm so defenseless right now.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:20.900
Are you sure?

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.710
You can do whatever you want.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.580
Then how about this?

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.960
Ouch!

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.320
How is it?

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.620
It's too much.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.340
Just kidding.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.630
Checkmate.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.240
Well?

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.260
You win.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.620
You're a sloppy player, Loserjima-kun.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.890
Please don't give me any unlucky nicknames.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:49.190
It's good luck for me since we're competing.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:49.900
You don't like it?

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.150
Of course not.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:55.030
Wanna go another round?

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:27.880
Hey, did you find him?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.370
No, not yet.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.380
This is so weird.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.700
How did he just disappear?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.200
It's creepy.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:38.220
Looks like they won't stop until they find you.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.640
How am I going to get out of here?

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.010
You have two choices.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.260
First, give up and turn yourself in.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.520
Second, live with me here for the rest of your life.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:54.770
Third, play some more shogi and wait a little longer.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.860
Weren't there <i>two</i> choices?

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:58.940
You don't want a third one?

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.940
Oh, no. I'll go with the third choice for now.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:05.030
And if it doesn't work out, I'll go with the second one.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.020
Are you sure about that?

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.540
What would my big sister think if she found out?

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.420
Hazuki-sensei has nothing to do with it.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.540
But you two kissed, right?

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:18.260
I told you that it was an accident!

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:22.890
What if <i>I</i> forced myself on you with a kiss?

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.890
Would you still call it an accident?

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:30.240
Kissjima-kun!

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:30.850
Yes?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.220
You make the first move this time.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:36.820
Okay.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.580
Can I ask you something?

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:46.960
What is it?

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.280
Did you ever hear the reason my sister left home?

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.370
The reason she left home?

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:58.060
She just holed up at home one day.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.130
She did?

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.720
She also stopped interacting with the entire family.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.510
I asked my parents why, but they weren't of any help.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:11.160
My sister kept quiet and wouldn't tell me anything.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.560
She went on like that until she left home.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.980
It's troubled my mother ever since.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.100
It still depresses her, even now.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.280
I want to do something, but I don't even know what happened.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.380
It seems like my sister is open with you,

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.290
so I thought she might have told you something about it.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.980
No. Sorry, but she's never mentioned it before.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.320
I see.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.020
Now's your chance.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:43.920
Okay!

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.430
Someone might be making rounds, so let's take the fire escape.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.660
You're a lifesaver.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:58.920
I had a lot of fun.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.920
Could we hang out again sometime?

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.800
Of course. I'd love to.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.820
And about what we discussed earlier...

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:10.980
Yeah, I'll ask Sensei about it when I have a chance.

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:13.250
No, not that.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:18.380
If I were to force myself on you with a kiss,

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:24.920
would you treat that as just an accident, too?

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:30.000
Um...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.240
Well?

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:32.980
I...

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:38.420
Hazuki-sensei!

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.700
I feel alive!

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.030
Hey, Yuu-kun, you want some?

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:54.870
Wai—

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.060
Gotcha.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.790
U-Um...

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.690
Sorry, sorry.

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:05.170
But that helped you cool down, didn't it?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:18.330
Oojima
Yuuki
Election
Headquarters<b></b>

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:22.700
Guys, did you hear? There was
a pervert at the campsite last night.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.570
P-Pervert? There was a p-pervert?!

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:28.100
He caused a ruckus and
kept a few girls up all night.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.040
We should've captured him and kicked his ass!

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.200
I was out like a light, so I didn't even notice.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.980
Non-chan says, "Early to bed, early to rise," so she didn't notice, either!

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:39.580
Staying up late is bad for your skin!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.900
You didn't notice anything, Prez?

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:43.960
N-No.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.510
Hazuki was drunk, so I had to take care of her.

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.960
I'm a heavy sleeper, so I didn't notice anything, either.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.050
What about you, Morishita-san?

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.680
I slept through it.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.680
I thought the camp dorm had very tight security,

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.350
but it's actually pretty dangerous, huh?

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:03.620
I bet some dumb girl brought him into the building.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.320
Who could that dumb girl be?

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.360
Y-Yeah, I wonder.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.980
It's time for some recreation!

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.120
Recreation?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.560
Recreation is an essential element of a camp!

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:21.840
We'll be doing a standard...

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.040
test of courage!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.800
Test of courage?

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.920
Well, the campaign work is going well, so we can probably afford to play around.

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.760
It was developed secretly in the event that it would be needed!

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.600
It's the "Freaky, destruction feature-equipped,

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.310
self-evolving creature exclusively built for test of courage," a.k.a...

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.060
"Bakeru-kun!"

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:49.040
As usual, I can't begin to imagine where your invention's shortened name comes from.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:53.320
Now, let's go give school ghost stories a try!

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.340
Hazuki-sensei?

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.680
That one was Aomi-san.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.280
Think they're okay?

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:19.360
Chisato?

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.880
Are you <i>that</i> worried about them?

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:24.700
Well, if they're screaming, of course I'd get worried.

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.360
That excuse won't work on me.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.780
What excuse?

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:43.120
The hell is that?

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.750
A Japanese toilet?

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.980
Oh, it's Hanako-san from that toilet girl myth.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.960
So a hand should emerge from inside...

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:54.660
L-Legs?

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.830
I don't get it.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.520
Hey! Chisa—

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.940
Wh-What are you doing?

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.700
Oh, no! It's so scary!

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.380
Save me, Yuuki!

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.150
Protect me!

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:12.260
What do you want me to do, exactly?

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.780
Why aren't you worried about me?

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:19.030
You were so worried about Hazuki and Isara earlier.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.560
It's hard to take this situation seriously.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.700
So you won't worry about me, huh?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.300
That's not what I said.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:28.040
It's the same as last night!

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.920
What? Last night?

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.460
What were you two up to?

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.380
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.450
I know it was you!

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:41.350
N-Nothing much. We were just playing some shogi.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:44.100
Shogi? Why would you play shogi with Hazuki?

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:47.520
Huh? Oh, with Hazuki-sensei. Right.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.100
Who else were you with?

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:51.720
Um... Well, yeah.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:54.140
I was with Hazuki-sensei.

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:57.820
But she got so drunk that she passed out, so I took her to her camp dorm.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:58.960
Really?

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.840
What's going on, Chisato?

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.460
You've been acting weird lately.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.060
I mean, yesterday...

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:22.220
You don't need act that way. You know I won't leave you.

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:26.460
I'm not going anywhere.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:29.800
I'll be with you whenever you need me.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.230
Yuuki...

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:35.860
But it's not <i>that</i> kind of love.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:40.110
You understand that, right?

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.250
I don't.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:52.630
I don't... understand.

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.630
Oojima-senpai!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.720
Looks like we caught up to you.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:01.140
Hey, wait!

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.220
Wait, Chisato!

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:20.580
I got to bathe in peace for once.

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.160
Hazuki-sensei?

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:28.400
Huh?

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:30.160
Oh, here comes the girl's bedroom intruder!

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:35.740
I-I was just mistaken for a pervert and almost caught, thanks to a certain someone!

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:36.880
Then Shinonome-san saved me—

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:40.500
Damn that Satsuki! She's crafty as hell.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:41.930
There's just no helping you.

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:44.580
Sensei.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:45.700
Hm?

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:49.300
Why do you hate Shinonome-san so much?

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:52.560
I wouldn't say that I hate her.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.680
Then do you hate your family?

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:59.400
Why did you leave them without—

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.740
Did Satsuki ask you to find out?

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.260
U-Um, well...

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:07.540
I knew booze was the only thing I could trust.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:10.400
I can't believe my little sister would make a cuckold of me.

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:12.680
That's <i>not</i> what's going on!

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.920
Give me a break from all the teasing already.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.240
You wouldn't even listen to me when I sincerely confessed.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:22.680
You never sincerely confessed anything to me.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.300
Should I do it now, then?

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:33.010
I love you, Yuu-kun.

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:34.900
Now, what's your response?

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:38.860
Ah... Well, of course I love you, too, Sensei!

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.860
You're trying to avoid this again?

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.980
I'm talking about the <i>romantic</i> kind of love.

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:46.520
That wasn't a joke, but a serious declaration of love.

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:52.280
I was holding back since I'm an adult and should know better.

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:54.460
Plus, I thought you had Chisato.

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:59.920
But if you're going to date Satsuki, that's a different story.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.740
No, it's not really...

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.920
Come on. Answer me already.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.970
Huh? Well...

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:10.620
It's hard for me to respond to your feelings so suddenly,

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.730
so could you give me some time to get back to you?

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:21.240
Hey, Satsuki?

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:22.500
It's me.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.070
Wanna fight to see who gets Yuu-kun?

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:30.240
Beat me and I'll even tell you what you want to know as a bonus prize.

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:31.360
How about it?

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.750
Let's have a good game.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:47.700
I'm surprised you agreed to this so easily.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:51.430
I thought it'd be a good opportunity to learn what really happened.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:54.930
But isn't <i>he</i> what you're really after?

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:59.000
Don't tease me!

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.080
You're so easy to read.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:06.380
You think that's enough to throw me off focus?

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:08.610
You must still be drunk.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:12.740
Yeah, I might even be drunk enough to kiss Yuu-kun again.

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:17.480
Oh, did that manage to rile you up?

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.960
You still have a lot to learn about love.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:22.880
I'm just not loose like you.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.120
Ever the pure maiden, huh?

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.090
I wonder which of them you take after.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:33.520
Did you know? Her mother is the second one.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:34.360
Huh?

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:36.430
Please don't talk about my mother.

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.560
She was my father's mistress,

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:42.100
but she became his wife after my mother passed away.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.440
Stop.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.500
Good for you, Satsuki.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.820
You got to be born after they tied the knot.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:48.660
Stop it.

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:51.120
If you were born before the marriage, you'd have been the mistress's child.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:51.960
Stop it!

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:56.000
If that happened, you wouldn't have been able to flaunt being from a well-established family.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:56.950
Stop it!

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.620
I bet you're glad that I left.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.920
Sh-Shinonome-san...

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:12.010
Are you forfeiting the match?

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:18.020
I'll take him.

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.040
Ouch!

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:25.070
Sensei...

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:26.320
Silver to 4I!

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:28.070
Rook to 1H, promotion!

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:29.480
Pawn to 2F!

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:30.780
You're still going?

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.700
What about you? Don't run.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.060
Wouldn't dream of it.

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:35.580
Knight to 3G, no promotion.

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.080
Just telling me your story won't cut it.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.360
Rook to 8H.

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:42.210
When I win, you'll go back home and apologize to Mother!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.440
You mean <i>if</i> you win.

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:46.460
Knight to 6G, check.

00:15:48.270 --> 00:15:49.590
Still think you can win?

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:51.720
Silver to 6G.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.720
Knight to 4I, promotion, check!

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:55.100
King to 6H!

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.100
Dragon to 4H, check!

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:02.320
What's wrong? Where'd all that spirit go?

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.860
Well, take your time.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.030
What's going on here?

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:10.580
She's thinking hard about her next move.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:12.680
Hey, got any beer?

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:14.340
Of course not!

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:18.580
Not very considerate, are you?

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:25.000
All right, then... Oh, yeah.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.760
I'll tell you a story so you don't get bored.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:28.840
A story?

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:32.280
It's from when Satsuki was little.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.760
One time, I hurt my head, and it left a mark.

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:38.140
Right here. Can you see it?

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:40.290
It's pretty big.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.890
It bled a lot, too.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.880
It was bad enough for people to say that I might need a blood transfusion.

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:46.810
<i>That</i> bad?

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:48.960
It was just people talking out of their asses.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.160
I got stitches and turned out fine.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:55.360
But there was a reason why the adults got so frantic.

00:16:56.750 --> 00:17:00.410
I have Rh negative blood.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:05.420
They were worried that there might not be enough blood for a transfusion.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:09.870
Then someone close came forward saying that they had the same blood type.

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.320
Can you guess who it was?

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:15.640
My mother is Rh negative.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:16.850
That's right.

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:19.600
No way... That can't be true!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:23.540
It <i>is</i> true. Your mother gave birth to me.

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:24.900
It was <i>her</i>.

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:25.850
No way...

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:31.480
Th-Then you and Shinonome-san are blood-related and share the same two parents?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.380
It could just be a coincidence!

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:37.520
A child can be born Rh negative even if the parents are both Rh positive!

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:39.410
There's even more undeniable proof.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:46.080
Long before I was born, my late mother

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.960
had her uterus removed due to an illness.

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:55.170
When I found out, our father resigned himself to telling me everything.

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.320
When my late mother became unable to bear children,

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:01.560
he was already having an
affair with Satsuki's mother.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:06.600
Many of his relatives pressured him to
abandon his wife, who couldn't bear children,

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:10.140
so he could marry his mistress.

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:11.060
That's just...

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:14.270
But he couldn't just abandon his wife.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:17.320
So he settled for having a baby with the second woman.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.640
That's me.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:21.830
I'm the mistress's child.

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:30.580
To fool the relatives, he took me in to raise as his legitimate child.

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:33.440
It must've been tough for his first wife.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:36.980
She may have even hated me deep down.

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:44.580
But I can only remember her showering me with love.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.440
She must have really loved me.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:52.780
With her body as weak as it was,
she eventually succumbed to her illness.

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:59.340
Before I could even mourn, the second wife came in,
and Satsuki was born not too long after.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:05.840
Since I got myself a cute sister, I chose to just get along with the family.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:11.710
But I couldn't keep that up after learning the truth.

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:16.180
I found out by accident when a drunk relative let it slip.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.340
It was more than just shocking.

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:22.260
I didn't know how to face my own family anymore.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:25.470
Half panicking, I struggled to figure out what to do,

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.850
and my confusion turned into rage.

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:35.560
I couldn't forgive anyone in the family.

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:37.160
So I left.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:41.140
I mean, if I just let it go...

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:46.440
If I let it all go and accept <i>her</i> as my biological mother...

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.660
What does that make my late mother?

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:56.260
We would have an authentic, blood-related family.

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:59.780
It'd be as though my late mother never existed in the first place.

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:03.800
But that's just wrong! I couldn't bear it!

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:06.320
What would her life have amounted to then?

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:08.540
She didn't even do anything wrong!

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:13.160
If I accepted the truth about our family,

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:17.900
it would... it would really be like she never mattered.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:23.790
That's why I'll never forgive that family.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:24.990
I've made up my mind.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:29.720
I only have one mother. The one who passed away.

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:34.280
That's the way it has been and always will be.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:42.280
I'm sorry! Onee-chan, I'm so sorry!

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:46.260
I had no idea.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.500
You've been through so much, and I...

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:53.440
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:54.760
I'm sorry.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:02.500
No one's blaming you, Satsuki.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:04.800
You really had nothing to do with it.

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.680
But... But...

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:08.540
Satsuki.

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:11.700
Onee-chan!

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:15.800
I'm so sorry.

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:29.300
He secretly met with Shinonome late at night?

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:32.450
Oojima is quite the troublemaker.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:35.960
If Shinonome were to use this against him...

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:40.400
No, if she were after something like that, she'd use the pervert incident.

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:48.900
It'd be troublesome if others found out about this.

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:50.820
That goes double for the enemies closest to us.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:55.540
The Public Safety Commissioner will return next week when his suspension ends.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:59.360
Prepare to hand the tasks over to him and keep an eye on the Katahira Faction.

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:00.020
Yes, sir!

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:24.530
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:28.490
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:32.630
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:32.630 --> 00:22:36.710
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:41.050
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:41.050 --> 00:22:45.210
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:45.210 --> 00:22:49.240
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:55.720
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:57.350 --> 00:23:02.360
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:06.530
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:08.720
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:12.420
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:14.950
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:19.210
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:23.090
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:28.850
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:36.720
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:45.980
You usually get cravings for sweets when you're thinking hard.

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:50.960
The brain runs on glucose, so they say that you may even perform better when you eat sweets.

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:54.620
But they also say that eating too many monosaccharides
can lead to a rapid rise in blood sugar levels,

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:57.660
which causes excessive secretion of insulin, making you sleepy.

00:23:57.660 --> 00:23:59.500
They say that's because
monosaccharides are absorbed quickly,

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.840
so the insulin secreted can decrease blood sugar levels too much

00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:04.740
and make you sleepy due to hypoglycemia.

00:24:04.740 --> 00:24:08.000
Next time, Episode 9: "Accident!"

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.930
Regardless, I still want sweets.
